<section class="nrh-section nrh-on-cream">
  <div class="wrap-narrow">
    <div class="nrh-eyebrow">The Narrow Road</div>
    <h2 class="nrh-section-title">Two Roads, and Only One Leads Home</h2>
    <p style="color:rgba(32,36,29,0.78); font-size:1.03rem; line-height:1.8; margin-bottom:18px;" data-reveal-scroll>Most of life is pulling you onto the wide road. It&rsquo;s crowded, it&rsquo;s easy to find, and everyone seems to be on it &mdash; but it doesn&rsquo;t actually lead anywhere good. It just keeps you busy, numb, or exhausted until it runs out.</p>
    <p style="color:rgba(32,36,29,0.78); font-size:1.03rem; line-height:1.8; margin-bottom:18px;" data-reveal-scroll>The narrow road is different. It&rsquo;s harder to find, and it costs you something &mdash; your pride, your control, the parts of your life you&rsquo;d rather keep to yourself. But it&rsquo;s the only road that actually leads home, because it&rsquo;s the road Jesus is walking with you on.</p>
    <p style="color:rgba(32,36,29,0.78); font-size:1.03rem; line-height:1.8;" data-reveal-scroll>You don&rsquo;t have to have your life together to get on it. You just have to be willing to turn.</p>
  </div>
</section><section class="nrh-gospel-band" id="gods-story">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="nrh-eyebrow">God&rsquo;s Story</div>
    <h2 class="nrh-gospel-title">It&rsquo;s Simpler Than You Think</h2>
    <p class="nrh-gospel-sub">Here&rsquo;s the whole thing, in four steps &mdash; no theology degree required.</p>
    <div class="nrh-gospel-steps">
      <div class="nrh-gospel-step" data-reveal-scroll>
  <span class="nrh-gospel-num">01</span>
  <div>
    <h3>You Were Made for More</h3>
    <p>You&rsquo;re not an accident. God made you on purpose, and He knows you completely &mdash; the parts you&rsquo;re proud of and the parts you hide. He didn&rsquo;t make you to be alone, numb, or stuck. He made you to know Him.</p>
  </div>
</div><div class="nrh-gospel-step" data-reveal-scroll>
  <span class="nrh-gospel-num">02</span>
  <div>
    <h3>Something Broke the Road</h3>
    <p>But every one of us has gone our own way. We&rsquo;ve chosen our own path over God&rsquo;s more times than we can count &mdash; that&rsquo;s what the Bible calls sin. It doesn&rsquo;t just break rules; it breaks the road, and it separates us from the God who made us.</p>
  </div>
</div><div class="nrh-gospel-step" data-reveal-scroll>
  <span class="nrh-gospel-num">03</span>
  <div>
    <h3>Jesus Is the Way Back</h3>
    <p>This is the part that changes everything. Jesus &mdash; God&rsquo;s own Son &mdash; stepped onto the broken road Himself. He lived the life we couldn&rsquo;t live, died the death we deserved, and rose again to prove that death doesn&rsquo;t get the final word. He is the way home.</p>
  </div>
</div><div class="nrh-gospel-step" data-reveal-scroll>
  <span class="nrh-gospel-num">04</span>
  <div>
    <h3>The Response Is Simple, Not Small</h3>
    <p>You don&rsquo;t earn your way onto this road. You just turn &mdash; away from running your own way, and toward Jesus &mdash; and believe He is who He said He is. That&rsquo;s it. That&rsquo;s the whole road.</p>
  </div>
</div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section><section class="nrh-section nrh-on-cream" id="prayer">
  <div class="wrap-narrow">
    <div class="nrh-eyebrow" style="text-align:center; justify-content:center; display:flex;">Your Next Step</div>
    <h2 class="nrh-section-title" style="text-align:center;">If You&rsquo;re Ready to Turn</h2>
    <p style="color:rgba(32,36,29,0.75); font-size:1.02rem; line-height:1.8; text-align:center; max-width:600px; margin:0 auto 36px;" data-reveal-scroll>This prayer isn&rsquo;t magic words, and praying it doesn&rsquo;t earn you anything. It&rsquo;s just you telling God, in your own way, what&rsquo;s already true in your heart. If it says what you mean, pray it &mdash; out loud or silently, right where you are.</p>

    <div class="nrh-prayer-card" data-reveal-scroll>
      <p class="nrh-prayer-text">Jesus, I believe You are who You say You are. I believe You died for me and rose again so I could be free. I&rsquo;m sorry for running my own way &mdash; today, I&rsquo;m turning around. Come into my life. Be my Savior. Be my Lord. I don&rsquo;t have this all figured out, but I&rsquo;m not walking away anymore. I&rsquo;m walking toward You, and toward home. Amen.</p>
    </div>

    <div style="text-align:center; margin-top:40px;" data-reveal-scroll>
      <p style="color:rgba(32,36,29,0.75); font-size:0.98rem; line-height:1.75; max-width:540px; margin:0 auto 22px;">If you just prayed that and meant it &mdash; whether it&rsquo;s the first time or the hundredth time you&rsquo;ve come back &mdash; Daniel would love to hear about it. You don&rsquo;t have to say much.</p>
      <a href="contact.html" class="nrh-btn-fill">Tell Daniel <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span></a>
    </div>
  </div>
